      "text": "To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\), we need to find a common denominator and then combine the fractions.\n\nFirst, we find the common denominator. The common denominator for the fractions \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i}\\) and \\(\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\) is \\((3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)\\). We recognize that \\((3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - (-25) = 9 + 25 = 34\\).\n\nSo, we rewrite each fraction with the common denominator 34:\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i)}{34} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)^2}{34},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i)}{34} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)^2}{34}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we expand the squares in the numerators:\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)^2 = 3^2 + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2 = 9 + 30i + 25i^2 = 9 + 30i + 25(-1) = 9 + 30i - 25 = -16 + 30i,\n\\]\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)^2 = 3^2 - 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2 = 9 - 30i + 25i^2 = 9 - 30i + 25(-1) = 9 - 30i - 25 = -16 - 30i.\n\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{-16 + 30i}{34} + \\frac{-16 - 30i}{34} = \\frac{(-16 + 30i) + (-16 - 30i)}{34} = \\frac{-16 + 30i - 16 - 30i}{34} = \\frac{-32}{34} = -\\frac{16}{17}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified form of the expression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{16}{17}}.\n\\]",
