      "text": "To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\), we will first simplify each fraction separately and then add the results.\n\nFirst, let's simplify \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i}\\). To do this, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is \\(3 + 5i\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} \\cdot \\frac{3 + 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i)}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)}.\n\\]\n\nThe denominator simplifies as follows:\n\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - (-25) = 9 + 25 = 34.\n\\]\n\nThe numerator simplifies as follows:\n\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2 = 9 + 30i + 25i^2 = 9 + 30i + 25(-1) = 9 + 30i - 25 = -16 + 30i.\n\\]\n\nSo, the first fraction simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{-16 + 30i}{34} = -\\frac{16}{34} + \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17}.\n\\]\n\nNext, let's simplify \\(\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\). Similarly, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the complex conjugate of the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} \\cdot \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 - 5i} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i)}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)}.\n\\]\n\nThe denominator simplifies as follows:\n\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i) = 9 - (5i)^2 = 9 - (-25) = 9 + 25 = 34.\n\\]\n\nThe numerator simplifies as follows:\n\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i) = 3^2 - 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2 = 9 - 30i + 25i^2 = 9 - 30i + 25(-1) = 9 - 30i - 25 = -16 - 30i.\n\\]\n\nSo, the second fraction simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{-16 - 30i}{34} = -\\frac{16}{34} - \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17}.\n\\]\n\nNow, we add the two simplified fractions:\n\n\\[\n-\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17} + \\left(-\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17}\\right) = -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17} = -\\frac{16}{17} + 0i = -\\frac{16}{17}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{16}{17}}.\n\\]",
